<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stafford</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stafford is the county town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/staffordshire">Staffordshire</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">English Midlands</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelflaed">Æthelflæd, Lady of the Mercians</a>, fortified it as a burh in 913 during her campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a>, and it became the centre of the shire created around it in the 10th century. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norman-conquest">Norman Conquest</a> a castle was built nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stafford.jpg" alt="Stafford" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Staffordshire County Council · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Staffordshire_Shire_Hall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
